{"title":"2025 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Amy the ant lives in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9bcf76cf936718b266bc4ea68b525ea852df68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangular grid of dots shown. From some dot <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, she can move to a dot that is either horizontally adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, diagonally adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a4f97ce27c2bb251b589501c8f83b8d33612b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{D}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />, or connected to D by a segment. In how many different ways can Amy visit every dot exactly once if she starts at the starred dot?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf29de6056d17a5ef9e83fd312878967593f9566.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); import geometry;  point P1=(1,1); point P2=(2,1); point P3=(3,1); point P4=(4,1); point P5=(5,1); point P6=(6,1); point P13=(7,1); point P15=(8,1); point P7=(1,2); point P8=(2,2); point P9=(3,2); point P10=(4,2); point P11=(5,2); point P12=(6,2); point P14=(7,2); point P16=(8,2);  draw(P15--P16);  dot(P1); dot(P2); dot(P3); dot(P4); dot(P5); dot(P6); dot(P7); dot(P8); dot(P9); dot(P10); dot(P11); dot(P12); dot(P13); dot(P14); dot(P15); dot(P16);  label(&quot;$\\star$&quot;,P1,dir(-135)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"52\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033643\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 30/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1290/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35298:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033643 and revision id 273719. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}